  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">In two sections, sewn back-to-back at the fold, each with a separate title: Spirit land: Arizona, and Spirit land: Oregon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The Arizona section includes the poem, "Sonoran desert unfolding," by Gary Paul Nabhan, and is printed on paper made from Arizona plants.  The Oregon section includes the poem, "Oregon reunion of the rare," by Kim Stafford, and is printed on paper made from Oregon plants. Each section lists endangered, threatened, and protected plants in those areas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">John Risseeuw made the paper enclosure from from "a mixture of Arizona and Oregon fibers plus soil and crushed shells"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">An edition of 50.</subfield>
